{
  "recommendations": {
    "W-001": {
      "fix": "Remove anonymous access to /api/Users by configuring the application's security filters to require authentication and authorization for this endpoint. Specifically, set the route to be accessible only to users with the 'admin' role, and test that unauthenticated requests receive a 401 or 403 response.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-002": {
      "fix": "For /rest/user/login, parameterize all SQL queries or use an ORM that prevents SQL injection. Implement prepared statements with parameter binding for the login query, and sanitize user input. Also, consider using a stored procedure if direct queries are necessary.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-003": {
      "fix": "Parameterize the search query in /api/Products. Use prepared statements or an ORM to avoid concatenating user input into SQL. Validate and sanitize the search parameter to ensure it matches expected format, and consider using a full-text search library if supported.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-004": {
      "fix": "Encode all user-supplied data on output in /search. Implement context-aware output encoding (e.g., HTML entity encoding) for the search term in the response. Also, set the Content-Security-Policy header to mitigate XSS.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-005": {
      "fix": "Implement strict authorization checks on /api/Addresss to ensure users can only access their own addresses. Replace direct object references with indirect ones or verify ownership before returning data. Use session-based user ID to filter queries.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-006": {
      "fix": "Restrict /rest/admin to authenticated users with an 'admin' role. Add a security filter or middleware that checks the user's role and denies access otherwise. Remove any hard-coded credentials or backdoors that might allow anonymous access.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-007": {
      "fix": "For /rest/user/whoami, ensure that the endpoint only returns information for the authenticated user. Verify that it does not leak sensitive data such as tokens or roles if accessed with insufficient privileges. Restrict access to authenticated users only.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-008": {
      "fix": "On /file-upload, restrict file types to a safe allowlist (e.g., images) and validate content, not just extension. Store uploaded files outside the web root, serve them with a Content-Disposition: attachment header, and scan for malware. Also, ensure the directory has no execute permissions.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-009": {
      "fix": "Sanitize and encode user input when storing and rendering complaints on /api/Complaints. Use output encoding when displaying stored data, and consider implementing a WAF or CSP to mitigate XSS. Validate input to strip script tags or use a rich-text sanitizer.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-010": {
      "fix": "For /rest/user/reset-password, make responses uniform for both existing and non-existing users. Return a generic message and use a generic email template. Also, implement rate limiting to prevent automated enumeration attempts.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-011": {
      "fix": "Secure /rest/admin/application-configuration by requiring authentication and authorization. This endpoint should only be accessible to administrators, and sensitive configuration data should be redacted or not returned at all. Use fine-grained access controls.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-012": {
      "fix": "For /register, implement a whitelist of allowed fields for user creation. Ignore any extra parameters in the request, and explicitly assign only expected fields like username, email, and password. Do not allow setting roles or other privileged attributes via mass assignment.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-013": {
      "fix": "Add rate limiting to /rest/user/login to prevent brute force attacks. Use a tool like Fail2ban or implement custom middleware to limit login attempts per IP and per user, with a lockout after several failed attempts.",
      "effort": "low"
    },
    "W-014": {
      "fix": "For /rest/wallet/balance, ensure the endpoint only returns the balance of the authenticated user and that it does not expose sensitive information like account numbers or tokens. Use TLS for all communications and avoid logging sensitive data.",
      "effort": "medium"
    },
    "W-015": {
      "fix": "For /rest/chatbot, treat all input as untrusted and never use it in template engines or system commands. Use an allowlist of commands or a sandboxed environment. Apply context-aware output encoding and input validation to block SSTI and injection attempts.",
      "effort": "high"
    }
  },
  "narrative": "The assessment revealed a broad attack surface with multiple high-severity vulnerabilities, though many were not fully proven due to time constraints and require further verification. The immediate priority should be addressing the SQL injection and XSS issues (W-002, W-003, W-004, W-009) as they can lead to data compromise. For the unproven findings, treat them as hypotheses and conduct targeted retesting as part of remediation. Confidence in these results is moderate; the untested findings (W-011 through W-015) are based on code review and configuration analysis, so verify them with automated tools or manual testing. Prioritize fixes that are low effort and high impact, such as securing unauth endpoints and adding rate limiting, to quickly reduce risk."
}

